    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'SpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsSetByTheEntityWithDefinedTimelinesExplanatoryTextBlock' (SpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsSetByTheEntityWithDefinedTimelinesExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Sustainability at Cipla is driven through our core purpose of 'Caring for Life'. Guided by this philosophy, we continue to advance our sustainability journey through purposeful actions that strengthen our environmental, social and governance impact.\n\nWith FY 2019-20 as the baseline year, we had established a set of ambitious sustainability goals for our India manufacturing operations (i.e. manufacturing units of Cipla Limited and all its wholly owned subsidiaries in India) to be achieved by December 2025. \n\nGoals (India manufacturing operations) 2025:\n\n1) 80% reduction in absolute Scope 1 (energy based) and Scope 2 emissions from baseline year FY 2019-20\n2) Water Neutrality\n3) Zero Waste to Landfill (“ZWTL”)\n4) 50% renewable energy\n5) Continuing zero fatality\n6) Full compliance with safe discharge targets established by AMR Industry Alliance ('AMRIA')\n\nHaving successfully met these targets, we are now advancing our commitment to Caring for Nature by building this momentum and setting up a new, more comprehensive set of sustainability goals to be achieved by 2030.\n\nEmbracing these renewed and enhanced commitments reflect our continued focus on responsible growth while amplifying our positive impact on society and the environment.\n\nNear term: 2030 Goals\n\n1) Environment:\na. Renewable Electricity share: 80% for India manufacturing operations\nb. GHG Emission (Scope-1 & 2)\n(i) 30% Absolute reduction (Scope-1 energy based and Scope 2) from baseline of FY 2023-24 for Global Operations\n(ii) Build capacity infrastructure for green propellants used in MDI\nc. Water Neutrality: Maintain ZWTL status for India manufacturing operations and expand coverage for ZWTL to overseas sites for US and One Africa\nd. AMR: One Antibiotic Product per Cipla India site certified as per AMR manufacturing standard\n\n2) Social:\na. Occupational Health & Safety: Zero Fatality year-on-year in manufacturing operations\nb. Diversity, Equity and Inclusion: Representation of women in Cipla Leadership Group at 20% or above, from a baseline year of FY 2024-25 at 17%\n\n3) Governance:\na. Responsible Procurement: 80% of our critical Indian suppliers to comply with Cipla ESG framework\n\nLong term: 2050 Goals\n\nEnvironment: To achieve Net Zero by 2050\n\nThe specific ESG commitments, goals and targets are provided on page no. 32 of Advancing Our Sustainability Vision. Other commitments, goals and targets are provided in respective capitals of the Integrated Annual Report FY 2025-26, wherever applicable.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: SpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsSetByTheEntityWithDefinedTimelinesExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: D_Principle1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'SpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsSetByTheEntityWithDefinedTimelinesExplanatoryTextBlock' (SpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsSetByTheEntityWithDefinedTimelinesExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Sustainability at Cipla is driven through our core purpose of 'Caring for Life'. Guided by this philosophy, we continue to advance our sustainability journey through purposeful actions that strengthen our environmental, social and governance impact.\n\nWith FY 2019-20 as the baseline year, we had established a set of ambitious sustainability goals for our India manufacturing operations (i.e. manufacturing units of Cipla Limited and all its wholly owned subsidiaries in India) to be achieved by December 2025. \n\nGoals (India manufacturing operations) 2025:\n\n1) 80% reduction in absolute Scope 1 (energy based) and Scope 2 emissions from baseline year FY 2019-20\n2) Water Neutrality\n3) Zero Waste to Landfill (“ZWTL”)\n4) 50% renewable energy\n5) Continuing zero fatality\n6) Full compliance with safe discharge targets established by AMR Industry Alliance ('AMRIA')\n\nHaving successfully met these targets, we are now advancing our commitment to Caring for Nature by building this momentum and setting up a new, more comprehensive set of sustainability goals to be achieved by 2030.\n\nEmbracing these renewed and enhanced commitments reflect our continued focus on responsible growth while amplifying our positive impact on society and the environment.\n\nNear term: 2030 Goals\n\n1) Environment:\na. Renewable Electricity share: 80% for India manufacturing operations\nb. GHG Emission (Scope-1 & 2)\n(i) 30% Absolute reduction (Scope-1 energy based and Scope 2) from baseline of FY 2023-24 for Global Operations\n(ii) Build capacity infrastructure for green propellants used in MDI\nc. Water Neutrality: Maintain ZWTL status for India manufacturing operations and expand coverage for ZWTL to overseas sites for US and One Africa\nd. AMR: One Antibiotic Product per Cipla India site certified as per AMR manufacturing standard\n\n2) Social:\na. Occupational Health & Safety: Zero Fatality year-on-year in manufacturing operations\nb. Diversity, Equity and Inclusion: Representation of women in Cipla Leadership Group at 20% or above, from a baseline year of FY 2024-25 at 17%\n\n3) Governance:\na. Responsible Procurement: 80% of our critical Indian suppliers to comply with Cipla ESG framework\n\nLong term: 2050 Goals\n\nEnvironment: To achieve Net Zero by 2050\n\nThe specific ESG commitments, goals and targets are provided on page no. 32 of Advancing Our Sustainability Vision. Other commitments, goals and targets are provided in respective capitals of the Integrated Annual Report FY 2025-26, wherever applicable.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: SpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsSetByTheEntityWithDefinedTimelinesExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: D_Principle2)"
  },
  {
