  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'PerformanceOfTheEntityAgainstTheSpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsAlongWithReasonsInCaseTheSameAreNotMetExplanatoryTextBlock' (PerformanceOfTheEntityAgainstTheSpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsAlongWithReasonsInCaseTheSameAreNotMetExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'The progress against the targets for our India manufacturing operations (i.e. manufacturing units of Cipla Limited and all its wholly owned subsidiaries in India) to be achieved by December 2025 with FY 2019-20 as the base year is outlined below.\n\n1) 82% reduction in absolute Scope 1 (energy based) and Scope 2 emissions from baseline year FY 2019-20 by December 2025\n2) Achieved 2.6 times water positive\n3) All India manufacturing operations are Zero Waste to Landfill (\"ZWTL\") certified with 24 units advanced from Platinum to Platinum+ certification.\n4) Two warehouses—one domestic in Pune and one international, Cipla Distribution Gateway (\"CDC\") in South Africa are ZWTL certified\n5) 84% renewable electricity\n6) Achieved zero fatality in our manufacturing operations\n7) Achieved full compliance with the safe discharge targets\n\nThe performance against specific ESG commitments, goals and targets is provided on page no. 32 of Advancing Our Sustainability Vision. Performance against other commitments, goals and targets, are provided in the respective capitals of the Integrated Annual Report FY 2025-26, wherever applicable.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: PerformanceOfTheEntityAgainstTheSpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsAlongWithReasonsInCaseTheSameAreNotMetExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: D_Principle8)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'PerformanceOfTheEntityAgainstTheSpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsAlongWithReasonsInCaseTheSameAreNotMetExplanatoryTextBlock' (PerformanceOfTheEntityAgainstTheSpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsAlongWithReasonsInCaseTheSameAreNotMetExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'The progress against the targets for our India manufacturing operations (i.e. manufacturing units of Cipla Limited and all its wholly owned subsidiaries in India) to be achieved by December 2025 with FY 2019-20 as the base year is outlined below.\n\n1) 82% reduction in absolute Scope 1 (energy based) and Scope 2 emissions from baseline year FY 2019-20 by December 2025\n2) Achieved 2.6 times water positive\n3) All India manufacturing operations are Zero Waste to Landfill (\"ZWTL\") certified with 24 units advanced from Platinum to Platinum+ certification.\n4) Two warehouses—one domestic in Pune and one international, Cipla Distribution Gateway (\"CDC\") in South Africa are ZWTL certified\n5) 84% renewable electricity\n6) Achieved zero fatality in our manufacturing operations\n7) Achieved full compliance with the safe discharge targets\n\nThe performance against specific ESG commitments, goals and targets is provided on page no. 32 of Advancing Our Sustainability Vision. Performance against other commitments, goals and targets, are provided in the respective capitals of the Integrated Annual Report FY 2025-26, wherever applicable.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: PerformanceOfTheEntityAgainstTheSpecificCommitmentsGoalsAndTargetsAlongWithReasonsInCaseTheSameAreNotMetExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: D_Principle9)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'StatementByDirectorResponsibleForTheBusinessResponsibilityReportHighlightingESGRelatedChallengesTargetsAndAchievementsExplanatoryTextBlock' (StatementByDirectorResponsibleForTheBusinessResponsibilityReportHighlightingESGRelatedChallengesTargetsAndAchievementsExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Sustainability is integral to how we operate and create long-term value. In India manufacturing operations3,\nwe have achieved an 82% reduction in Scope 1 (energy based) and Scope 2 emissions against target of 80% reduction from FY 2019–20 baseline, with 84% renewable electricity use. We have maintained our water-positive status at 2.6 times through inhouse measures and impactful community-led initiatives and continue to strengthen circularity with Zero Waste to Landfill certification across all India manufacturing operations and two warehouses. Our progress in climate, biodiversity, and antimicrobial resistance is reflected in a DJSI score of 81 and our inclusion in the 2026 Dow Jones Best-in-Class World Index. Having successfully met our 2025 target, we are now advancing our commitment to Caring for Nature by building this momentum and setting up a new, more comprehensive set of sustainability goals to be achieved by 2030 and Net-Zero by 2050. We are also advancing green propellants for our respiratory portfolio, supported by manufacturing capabilities in India and the US. Through these efforts we remain committed to reducing our environmental footprint while prioritising patient health and safety.\n\nOn employee safety, we continue to reinforce our safety culture through disciplined adherence to life-saving rules, stronger hazard identification and risk management practices, and deeper leadership engagement across our sites. We remain unwavering in our commitment to the highest safety standards.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: StatementByDirectorResponsibleForTheBusinessResponsibilityReportHighlightingESGRelatedChallengesTargetsAndAchievementsExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfTheHighestAuthorityResponsibleForImplementationAndOversightOfTheBusinessResponsibilityPolicyExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfTheHighestAuthorityResponsibleForImplementationAndOversightOfTheBusinessResponsibilityPolicyExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Mr Umang Vohra, Managing Director and Global Chief Executive Officer (\"MD & GCEO\") (DIN: 02296740). Mr Achin Gupta (DIN: 09491674) appointed as MD & GCEO, in place of Mr Umang Vohra, w.e.f. 1st April, 2026.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfTheHighestAuthorityResponsibleForImplementationAndOversightOfTheBusinessResponsibilityPolicyExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DoesTheEntityHaveASpecifiedCommitteeOfTheBoardOrDirectorResponsibleForDecisionMakingOnSustainabilityRelatedIssues' (DoesTheEntityHaveASpecifiedCommitteeOfTheBoardOrDirectorResponsibleForDecisionMakingOnSustainabilityRelatedIssues) is 'Yes'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DoesTheEntityHaveASpecifiedCommitteeOfTheBoardOrDirectorResponsibleForDecisionMakingOnSustainabilityRelatedIssues, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfSpecifiedCommitteeOfTheBoardOrDirectorResponsibleForDecisionMakingOnSustainabilityRelatedIssuesExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfSpecifiedCommitteeOfTheBoardOrDirectorResponsibleForDecisionMakingOnSustainabilityRelatedIssuesExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Yes. Our Investment and Risk Management Committee (\"IRMC\") is responsible for periodically reviewing environmental, social and governance (\"ESG\") / sustainability matters pertaining to the Company. The IRMC composition as on 31st March, 2026 is as follows:\n\nMr Robert Stewart (Chairperson)*; DIN: 03515778; Independent Director\nMr Kamil Hamied (Member); DIN: 00024292; Non-Executive Director\nMr Umang Vohra (Member)**; DIN: 02296740; MD & GCEO\nMr Abhijit Joshi (Member); DIN: 07115673; Non-Executive Director\nMr P R Ramesh (Member); DIN: 01915274; Independent Director\n\n* Dr Mandar Vaidya designated as Chairperson w.e.f 1st April, 2026. Mr Robert Stewart continued as member.\n** Mr Umang Vohra ceased to be a member w.e.f. 1st April, 2026. Mr Achin Gupta appointed as a member w.e.f. 1st April, 2026'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfSpecifiedCommitteeOfTheBoardOrDirectorResponsibleForDecisionMakingOnSustainabilityRelatedIssuesExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
