  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'AreThePremisesOrOfficesOfTheEntityAccessibleToDifferentlyAbledEmployeesAndWorkers' (AreThePremisesOrOfficesOfTheEntityAccessibleToDifferentlyAbledEmployeesAndWorkers) is 'Yes'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: AreThePremisesOrOfficesOfTheEntityAccessibleToDifferentlyAbledEmployeesAndWorkers, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DoesTheEntityHaveAnEqualOpportunityPolicyAsPerTheRightsOfPersonsWithDisabilitiesAct2016' (DoesTheEntityHaveAnEqualOpportunityPolicyAsPerTheRightsOfPersonsWithDisabilitiesAct2016) is 'Yes'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DoesTheEntityHaveAnEqualOpportunityPolicyAsPerTheRightsOfPersonsWithDisabilitiesAct2016, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkOfEqualOppertunityPolicyTextBlock' (WebLinkOfEqualOppertunityPolicyTextBlock) is 'The Company has an Equal Opportunity Policy that upholds the principles of fairness, inclusion and non-discrimination, in line with the requirements of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016. The Policy reinforces the Company’s commitment to providing equitable opportunities and ensuring a respectful\nand inclusive work environment for all employees, including persons with disabilities. The Policy prohibits discrimination on any grounds, including disability and promotes equal access to employment, career development, training and workplace resources through unbiased hiring practices. Weblink of the\nPolicy:https://www.cipla.com/sites/default/files/2023-07/'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkOfEqualOppertunityPolicyTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForTheFollowingCategoriesOfEmployeesAndWorker' (IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForTheFollowingCategoriesOfEmployeesAndWorker) is 'true'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForTheFollowingCategoriesOfEmployeesAndWorker, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentWorkers' (IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentWorkers) is 'true'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentWorkers, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentWorkersExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentWorkersExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Yes. The Company has #WeAreListening Grievance Redressal Committee which is committed to addressing\nemployees and workers concerns promptly and effectively. Guided by our Code of Conduct and Employee\nGrievance Policy, the framework provides clear procedures for raising issues, helping cultivate trust,\ntransparency and accountability across the organisation.\n\nIn India, a self-reporting system enables employees to communicate concerns directly with leadership,\nfacilitating transparency and timely resolution. In South Africa, Sub-Saharan Africa and the Cipla Global\nAccess (One Africa) regions, grievance management aligns with internal policies as well as the Employment\nEquity Act, ensuring fairness and regulatory compliance. In the United States, the Open Door Policy\nempowers employees to raise concerns directly with management or the HR team.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentWorkersExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentWorkers' (IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentWorkers) is 'true'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentWorkers, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentWorkersExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentWorkersExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Yes. The Company has #WeAreListening Grievance Redressal Committee which is committed to addressing\nemployees and workers concerns promptly and effectively. Guided by our Code of Conduct and Employee\nGrievance Policy, the framework provides clear procedures for raising issues, helping cultivate trust,\ntransparency and accountability across the organisation.\nIn India, a self-reporting system enables employees to communicate concerns directly with leadership,\nfacilitating transparency and timely resolution. In South Africa, Sub-Saharan Africa and the Cipla Global\nAccess (One Africa) regions, grievance management aligns with internal policies as well as the Employment\nEquity Act, ensuring fairness and regulatory compliance. In the United States, the Open Door Policy\nempowers employees to raise concerns directly with management or the HR team.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentWorkersExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentEmployees' (IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentEmployees) is 'true'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentEmployees, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentEmployeesExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentEmployeesExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Yes. The Company has #WeAreListening Grievance Redressal Committee which is committed to addressing\nemployees and workers concerns promptly and effectively. Guided by our Code of Conduct and Employee\nGrievance Policy, the framework provides clear procedures for raising issues, helping cultivate trust,\ntransparency and accountability across the organisation.\nIn India, a self-reporting system enables employees to communicate concerns directly with leadership,\nfacilitating transparency and timely resolution. In South Africa, Sub-Saharan Africa and the Cipla Global\nAccess (One Africa) regions, grievance management aligns with internal policies as well as the Employment\nEquity Act, ensuring fairness and regulatory compliance. In the United States, the Open Door Policy\nempowers employees to raise concerns directly with management or the HR team.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForPermanentEmployeesExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentEmployees' (IsThereAMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentEmployees) is 'true'.",
