  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentEmployeesExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentEmployeesExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Yes. The Company has #WeAreListening Grievance Redressal Committee which is committed to addressing\nemployees and workers concerns promptly and effectively. Guided by our Code of Conduct and Employee\nGrievance Policy, the framework provides clear procedures for raising issues, helping cultivate trust,\ntransparency and accountability across the organisation.\nIn India, a self-reporting system enables employees to communicate concerns directly with leadership,\nfacilitating transparency and timely resolution. In South Africa, Sub-Saharan Africa and the Cipla Global\nAccess (One Africa) regions, grievance management aligns with internal policies as well as the Employment\nEquity Act, ensuring fairness and regulatory compliance. In the United States, the Open Door Policy\nempowers employees to raise concerns directly with management or the HR team.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfMechanismAvailableToReceiveAndRedressGrievancesForOtherThanPermanentEmployeesExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WhetherAnOccupationalHealthAndSafetyManagementSystemHasBeenImplementedByTheEntity' (WhetherAnOccupationalHealthAndSafetyManagementSystemHasBeenImplementedByTheEntity) is 'Yes'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WhetherAnOccupationalHealthAndSafetyManagementSystemHasBeenImplementedByTheEntity, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfOccupationalHealthAndSafetyManagementSystemExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfOccupationalHealthAndSafetyManagementSystemExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Yes. At Cipla, we are committed to maintaining the highest standards of occupational health and safety across our operations. Our comprehensive EHS&S Policy, aligned with statutory requirements, including ISO 14001 and ISO 45001 standards, as well as global best practices, provides a robust framework to monitor both qualitative and quantitative objectives and targets. These include reducing incidents, ensuring regulatory compliance, protecting the environment, and conserving energy, among others. \n\nFurther details are available on page no. 88 of Human Capital.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfOccupationalHealthAndSafetyManagementSystemExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DesclosureOfTheProcessesUsedToIdentifyWorkRelatedHazardsAndAssessRisksOnARoutineAndNonRoutineBasisByTheEntityExplanatoryTextBlock' (DesclosureOfTheProcessesUsedToIdentifyWorkRelatedHazardsAndAssessRisksOnARoutineAndNonRoutineBasisByTheEntityExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'We are committed to providing a safe and healthy workplace, recognising its importance for employee well-being and operational excellence. In line with ISO 45001, each site conducts an annual Occupational Safety and Health (\"OHS\") Hazard Identification and Risk Assessment (\"HIRA\") covering both routine and non-routine activities. While most of the routine activities undergo a structure HIRA, Non routine activities are undertaken with JSA/ Permit to work ensuring adequate risk assessment. All of our operational sites have completed an employee health and safety risk assessment in FY 2025-26. This process involves process owners, safety professionals, engineers and workers, ensuring comprehensive hazard identification and effective risk control. \n\nFurther details are available on page no. 88 of Human Capital.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DesclosureOfTheProcessesUsedToIdentifyWorkRelatedHazardsAndAssessRisksOnARoutineAndNonRoutineBasisByTheEntityExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WhetherYouHaveProcessesForWorkersToReportTheWorkRelatedHazardsAndToRemoveThemselvesFromSuchRisks' (WhetherYouHaveProcessesForWorkersToReportTheWorkRelatedHazardsAndToRemoveThemselvesFromSuchRisks) is 'Yes'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WhetherYouHaveProcessesForWorkersToReportTheWorkRelatedHazardsAndToRemoveThemselvesFromSuchRisks, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DoTheEmployeesOrWorkerOfTheEntityHaveAccessToNonOccupationalMedicalAndHealthcareServices' (DoTheEmployeesOrWorkerOfTheEntityHaveAccessToNonOccupationalMedicalAndHealthcareServices) is 'Yes'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DoTheEmployeesOrWorkerOfTheEntityHaveAccessToNonOccupationalMedicalAndHealthcareServices, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DescribeTheMeasuresTakenByTheEntityToEnsureASafeAndHealthyWorkPlaceExplanatoryTextBlock' (DescribeTheMeasuresTakenByTheEntityToEnsureASafeAndHealthyWorkPlaceExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'The entity ensures a safe and healthy workplace through a robust Environment, Health and Safety (\"EHS\") framework, anchored by a formally implemented EHS&S Policy aligned with statutory requirements, ISO 14001 and ISO 45001 standards, and global best practices. Adequate full-time safety professionals are deployed at all sites with clearly defined roles and responsibilities. Regular EHS training programs, including annual refresher sessions, are conducted for all employees and contractors to ensure awareness and adherence to safety protocols and obligations. We also place strong emphasis on employee participation, encouraging the workforce to actively contribute to safety-related decisions. Employees and contractors are represented across unit-level, site-level, and contractor EHS committees, ensuring inclusive participation from all functions. Additionally, committees such as the Canteen Committee and Transport Committee provide structured platforms for dialogue and collaborative problem-solving. These initiatives collectively foster a culture of shared responsibility and continuous improvement in workplace safety.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DescribeTheMeasuresTakenByTheEntityToEnsureASafeAndHealthyWorkPlaceExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfAnyCorrectiveActionTakenOrUnderwayToAddressSafetyRelatedIncidentsOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfAnyCorrectiveActionTakenOrUnderwayToAddressSafetyRelatedIncidentsOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'The entity addresses safety related incidents through a structured process of immediate reporting, investigation within defined timelines and corrective action. All incidents and near misses are promptly reported, undergo an initial investigation and are followed by a formal root cause analysis (\"RCA\") conducted by a designated RCA team. Corrective and Preventive Actions (“CAPA”) are defined, implemented and tracked, with closure verified by the Site EHS Head. Issues requiring broader intervention are escalated as global CAPA for deployment across all sites, which is also tracked till closure. All events/ incidents such as unsafe acts / conditions, high potential incidents, dangerous occurrences, spills and process safety events are reviewed and investigated to ensure right CAPA viz. retraining, updated risk assessments and strengthened engineering, and administrative controls etc., to minimise repeated incidents..'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfAnyCorrectiveActionTakenOrUnderwayToAddressSafetyRelatedIncidentsOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'PercentageOfHealthAndSafetyPracticesOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedP3' (PercentageOfHealthAndSafetyPracticesOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedP3) is '0.79' xbrli:pure.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: PercentageOfHealthAndSafetyPracticesOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedP3, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'PercentageOfWorkingConditionsOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedP3' (PercentageOfWorkingConditionsOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedP3) is '0.38' xbrli:pure.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: PercentageOfWorkingConditionsOfYourPlantsAndOfficesThatWereAssessedP3, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'NotesPrinciple3ExplanatoryTextBlock' (NotesPrinciple3ExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Under essential indicator 1(a) and (b) - The data is specific to Cipla Limited and its Indian subsidiaries. However, please note that the total column has been automatically updated using information from employees and workforce data provided in question no. 25 of Section A of the General Disclosure. For accurate details, please refer to the Annual Report, where the disclosure with the correct total column is provided. \nUnder essential indicator 1(1) and 1(b) This data is specific to Cipla Limited and its Indian Subsidiaries\n\nUnder essential indicator 1(c) - The data is specific to Cipla Limited. \n\nUnder essential indicator 2 - This data is specific to permanent employees and workers of Cipla Limited and its Indian subsidiaries excluding Jay Precision Pharmaceutical Private Limited. \n\nUnder essential indicator 5 - This data pertains to permanent employees and workers of Cipla Limited and Indian subsidiaries. During FY 2025-26 parental leave was not availed by any of the permanent workers\n\n Under essential indicator 7 - None of our permanent employees are part of any associations / unions. \n\nUnder essential indicator 8 - The data for Health and safety measures are based on average no. of workforce trained. Since there is no separate column for average total workforce trained during the percentage was calculated by dividing the average number of male/female employees, respectively,  by the total workforce. This data includes employees/workers who were active and separated during the year. \n\nUnder essential indicator 9 - Performance appraisal is conducted for all employees who have joined on or before 31st December,2025 and trainees confirmed on or before 31st December, 2025. Further, the employee must be on the payroll of the organisation as on 31st  March, 2026. However, please note that the total column has been automatically updated using information from employees and workforce data provided in question no. 8 of Principe 3. For accurate details, please refer to the Annual Report, where the disclosure with the correct total column is provided\n\nUnder essential indicator 11 - Lost Time Injury Frequency Rate (LTIFR) = (No. of lost time injuries in FY x 10,00,000)/(Total hours worked by all staff in same FY).'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: NotesPrinciple3ExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
